PRO_0449,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"5. It is most respectfully submitted that a complaint Section 12(l)(c) of the Consumer Protection Act read wit Order I Rule 8 of the Code of Civil Procedure can be fil where there are numerous consumers having the ""same interest"" i.e. a common grievance against the same perso the complaint is filed on behalf of or for the benefit o numerous consumers, and seeking same relief for all of t It is submitted that the all the buyers of the flat cann treated at par with each other as such most of the Complainants are investors whereas some of them may be genuine consumers. Thus in absence of the element of ""sa interest"" the present Complaint in the representative ca deserves to be dismissed. The Complainants thus ought to approach a civil court to address its grievance. On this alone the present application under 12(l)(c) deserves to dismissed.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,
PRO_0450,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"6. Admittedly, the Complainants herein have sought file the present Complaint for and on behalf of all cust of the Answering Opposite Party/Respondent who have made a booking for a flat in Indiabulls Greens, Village Kon, As admitted by the Complainants in the Complaint the fac and circumstances pertaining to each booking differs fro case to case as different customers have purchased diffe flats from the Answering Opposite Party/Respondent at different points of time ranging over the past decade, a different rates and have made pro rata payments to diffe extents with or without defaults therein. It is, therefo submitted that by no stretch of imagination it can be sa the numerous customers of the Answering Opposite Party/Respondent stand on a similar footing with respect each other. It is therefore submitted that the present Complaint is not maintainable as the cause of action has arisen till date. It is further submitted that the Compl have approached this Hon'ble Commission with malafide intentions of making unlawful gains and therefore no permission shall be given to file the present Complaint short ground alone and the present application ought to dismissed.  Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed By:SUNIL SINGH NEGI CM(M) 664/2018 Signing Date:02.05.2022 15:58:14",PROPERTY,,,,,,,
