PRO_0455,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"7. In order to find out whether or not the instan complaint fits into the requirements of Section 12(1) Act, I have carefully perused the complaint, in parti prayer clause. On reading of the complaint as also th Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed By:SUNIL SINGH NEGI CM(M) 664/2018 Signing Date:02.05.2022 15:58:14 clause, it is clear that instant complaint has bee respect of a booking of development project involvi numerous consumers and the complainants have filed instant complaint against the opposite parties as a action on their behalf and also on behalf of and fo of all other consumers similarly placed and having interest in the outcome of the complaint. Merely be some of the complainants are NRls, will not make th persons of a different class. If the claims of some existing complainants have already been satisfied, not get any relief subject to the evidence. Thus, i requirements of Section 12(1)(c) of the Act are ful case and accordingly, I allow the application under 12(1)(c) of the Act and permit the complainants to with the complaint as a class action.  (Emphasis Lucina Land Development Ltd vs Union Of India & Ors on 27 April, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/13785167/ 14",PROPERTY,,,,,,,
