PRO_1039,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"8. What is required i sameness of interest in the outcome of the complaint, but same interest with respect to the grievances of the complainants an deficiencies in service that the complaints claimed to have su the instance of the opposite party. It is only then, that the Protection Forum could assess the correctness of the allegatio deficiency of service on the part of the opposite party vis-a- complainants. Unless the consumers who have sameness of intere respect of their grievances vis-a-vis the opposite party were immediately identifiable from the complaint, the complaint can maintained as a class action covering the interest of all such consumers.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1040,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"7. I am, therefore, unable to subscribe to the view expre learned NCDRC in paras 5 to 7 of the impugned order dated 16 t 2018.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1041,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"8. In my view, the complaint, as filed, does not indicate in respect of 51 complainants who were before the learned NCDR there is  sameness of interest  as could permit the complaint maintained as a class action covering their grievances vis-a-v petitioners. The pleadings in the compliant, are not suffic enable the Court to assess the number of complainants who woul have sameness of interest, in their grievances vis-a-vis the p It cannot, therefore, be said that the consolidated claim of s Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed By:SUNIL SINGH NEGI CM(M) 664/2018 Pa Signing Date:02.05.2022 15:58:14 complainants who would have sameness of interest would be in of   1 crore. Lucina Land Development Ltd vs Union Of India & Ors on 27 April, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/13785167/ 37",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1042,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"0. Per consequence, the complaint filed by the petitioners applying the law laid down in Brigade Enterprises18, and on th of the pleadings contained in the complaint, be maintained as action in respect of all the allottees of the Indiabulls Green Project or even in respect of the 51 complainants who approach learned NCDRC.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1043,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"1. The complaint would, therefore, necessarily have to be dismissed, as, in the manner in which it is filed, it is not e that the complaint is maintainable before the learned NCDRC.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1044,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"2. Having said that, however, this order would not preclude complainants from filing a proper complaint, keeping in mind t observations contained hereinabove, as a class action proceedi under Section 12(1)(c) or otherwise, before the appropriate fo which might even be the learned NCDRC. Any such complaint, if when filed, would be decided by the concerned forum in accorda with law and keeping in view the observations contained in the judgment. Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed By:SUNIL SINGH NEGI CM(M) 664/2018 P Signing Date:02.05.2022 15:58:14 Conclusion",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1045,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"3. In view of the aforesaid, the petition is allowed. The i order of the learned NCDRC is quashed and set aside. The compl filed by the complainants before the learned NCDRC is also dismissed, reserving liberty as recorded in para 52 supra.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
