PRO_1499,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"6. For all these reasons, I am of the opinion that the righ petitioners, to approach this Court under Article 227 of the Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed By:SUNIL SINGH NEGI CM(M) 664/2018 Pag Signing Date:02.05.2022 15:58:14 Constitution of India cannot be affected by the remedy of app Supreme Court available under Section 23 of the Consumer Prote Act.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1500,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"7. Having said that, it is also clear that any party which invoke the jurisdiction of the High Court under Article 227 su itself to the rigours of the provision and to the restrictions The High Court, under Article 227, cannot examine the matter w the same latitude as would be available to a Court which exerc appellate jurisdiction. Lucina Land Development Ltd vs Union Of India & Ors on 27 April, 2022 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/13785167/ 21",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1501,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"8. The contention of Mr Piyush Singh that Article 227 of t Constitution of India ought not to be invoked by the petitione remedy of appeal, against the impugned order of the learned NC lay to the Supreme Court under Section 23 of the 1986 Act, is fallacious on another count as well, which somewhat pre-empts discussion that is to follow hereinafter. Section 23 provides appeal against a decision of the NCDRC in exercise of the powe conferred on it by Section 21(a)(i). Section 21 deals jurisdiction of the learned NCDRC. Sub-section (a)(i) of Secti vests jurisdiction in the learned NCDRC to entertain complaint the value of the goods or services and compensation, if any, e 1 crore. The respondents have valued their complaint in excess crore on the premise that the complaint is maintainable as a c action proceeding on behalf of all the allottees of units in t As I proceed to hold hereinafter, however, the pleadings in th Complaint do not make out a case for justified institution of Complaint as a class action proceeding for all the allottees i Signature Not Verified Digitally Signed By:SUNIL SINGH NEGI CM(M) 664/2018 Signing Date:02.05.2022 15:58:14 project, or even for the 51 complainants before the learned N Unless the number of consumers having ""sameness of interest"" i manifest from the pleadings in the Complaint, in the manner envisaged by law and as stipulated by the Supreme Court in Bri Enterprises Ltd. v. Anil Kumar Virmani18, it is not possible t that the cumulative value of the goods or services, or the compensation claimed, by all such consumers having sameness of interest, would exceed   1 crore. The very maintainability of Complaint before the learned NCDRC, under Section 21(a)(i) is, therefore, questionable. If Section 21(a)(i) is not applicable Section 23.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1502,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"9. Where the justifiability of the invocation, by the the jurisdiction of the learned NCDRC under Section 21(a)(i) i in doubt, it is obviously not open to the respondents to cite availability of an alternate remedy to the petitioners under S as a ground to non-suit them under Article 227 of the Constitu India. A plea of alternate appellate remedy, predicated on err invocation of original jurisdiction of the Court or Tribunal b obviously has to fail.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
PRO_1503,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"0. Even on facts, therefore, the assertions in the Com the respondents do not make out a case of availability, to the petitioners, of an alternate remedy",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
