PRO_1505,Lucina Land Development vs Union of India,"2. An authoritative pronouncement, on the maintainabil action complaints, under Section 35(1)(c)19 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, which is in pari materia and in haec ver Section 12(1)(c)2 of the 1986 Act, is available in the judgmen Supreme Court in Brigade Enterprises18. 33. 91 purchasers of 51 apartments in a residential com in that case, permitted, by the learned NCDRC to file a class consumer complaint in a representative capacity under Section 35(1)(c) of the 2019 Act, on behalf of and for the benefit of 1000 purchasers. Aggrieved by the said decision, Brigade Enter the builder, appealed to the Supreme Court.",PROPERTY,,,,,,,,
